# infra/.env — AI sidecar real-model credentials (OPT-IN).
#
# Copy to infra/.env and fill in to flip the sidecar from canned mock to a real
# model. With this file absent (or the key blank), the sidecar serves the
# deterministic canned generators and the demo path is unchanged — nothing
# breaks without credentials.
#
# docker compose reads infra/.env automatically (same dir as the compose file).
# Both VLM (/facts/draft -> image recognition + listing copy) and the auctioneer (/llm/auctioneer)
# flip together with one key.

# ── Volcengine Ark / Doubao (recommended — on-theme, free quota) ──
# 1. Console: https://console.volcengine.com/ark  -> complete real-name verification -> enable online inference
# 2. Create TWO inference endpoints — one per side. DO NOT reuse one
#    ep for both: a shared ep is a shared rate-limit queue, so the
#    high-frequency auctioneer backlogs the intro path (the "AI intro generation is slow"
#    symptom). Each ep gives an id like ep-2026xxxx-xxxxx.
#
#    · ARK_VLM_MODEL — pick a FAST MULTIMODAL model (doubao-seed-1.6-flash
#      class: vision input + TPOT ~10ms). One call reads the product image AND
#      writes the human intro copy; a thinking-class model (seed-1.6/2.0
#      thinking) burns seconds before the first token and the frontend's 12s
#      refine window expires → sellers only ever see the template.
#    · ARK_LLM_MODEL — text ep for auctioneer commentary; flash class too
#      (commentary is real-time flavor — late bubbles are worthless).
# 3. API key: Ark console -> API Key management.
ARK_API_KEY=
ARK_VLM_MODEL=        # FAST multimodal ep (doubao-seed-1.6-flash class) for /facts/draft image recognition + copy
ARK_LLM_MODEL=        # text ep for /llm/auctioneer — a DIFFERENT ep than VLM
# ARK_BASE_URL defaults to Beijing Ark; only set to override region for BOTH sides.
# ARK_BASE_URL=https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com/api/v3

# ── Optional per-side tuning ──
# Split providers per side (e.g. VLM on Ark, LLM on self-hosted Ollama):
# ARK_VLM_BASE_URL=
# ARK_LLM_BASE_URL=
# Per-side timeout in ms (sidecar default 30000 — sized for thinking models).
# With flash-class endpoints tighten so failures fall back to canned fast:
# ARK_VLM_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# ARK_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=6000

# ── Open-source path (optional "open-source model integration" - zero key, self-hosted) ──
# Same OpenAI-compatible adapter; point it at Ollama/vLLM instead of Ark.
# Example (Ollama running Qwen2.5 on the worker):
#   ARK_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#   ARK_API_KEY=ollama            # Ollama ignores the key but the adapter needs non-empty
#   ARK_VLM_MODEL=qwen2.5-vl:7b   # vision-capable — the intro copy needs to SEE the image
#   ARK_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b

# Filling the creds above enables BOTH VLM facts+intro and auctioneer commentary.
# VLM_MODE is an explicit kill-switch ONLY: set it to "mock" to force canned VLM
# facts even when a key is present. Leave it unset/blank to let the key decide.
# VLM_MODE=mock
